{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WuR5vEKL2j2g9cn7z1ai5A","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Brute-force check of the empty-pair lemma behind the derived first-moment bound\n(reports/random_graph_pathwidth_survey.md §1.4; paper1/todo.md \"Lean the derived random-graph\nbounds\", step one): for every graph on ≤ N vertices,\n\n    pw(G) ≥ n − 2·s*(G) − 2,   s*(G) = max over A ⊆ V of min(|A| − 1, n − |N[A]|),\n\ni.e. a layout of vertex separation k yields a set A with |A| ≥ s + 1 having at least s vertices\noutside its closed neighbourhood, s = ⌈(n − k)/2⌉ − 1 (the suffix at the position after the last\none where the suffix-free prefix is no larger than the suffix).  Also the weaker rounding the\nsurvey states, s'(G) = max_A min(|A|, n − |N[A]|) ≥ ⌈(n − k)/2⌉ − 1, i.e. pw ≥ n − 2s' − 2.\nPathwidth by the vertex-separation subset DP; graphs from nauty-geng.\n    python3 check.py --max-n 9 --workers 16\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse, subprocess, sys, collections\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/home/al/dev/MOSP\")\n\n\ndef parse_g6(line):\n    b = line.strip().encode(); n = b[0] - 63; bits = []\n    for ch in b[1:]:\n        v = ch - 63; bits += [(v >> i) & 1 for i in range(5, -1, -1)]\n    adj = [0] * n; k = 0\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(j):\n            if bits[k]: adj[i] |= 1 << j; adj[j] |= 1 << i\n            k += 1\n    return n, adj\n\n\ndef vs(n, adj):\n    full = (1 << n) - 1\n    # boundary b(S) = |N(S) \\ S|; f(S) = min_{v in S} max(f(S - v), b(S))\n    nb = [0] * (1 << n); f = [0] * (1 << n)\n    for S in range(1, 1 << n):\n        low = S & -S; v = low.bit_length() - 1\n        nb[S] = nb[S ^ low] | adj[v]\n        b = bin(nb[S] & ~S & full).count(\"1\")\n        best = n; T = S\n        while T:\n            low = T & -T; T ^= low\n            c = f[S ^ low]\n            if c < best: best = c\n        f[S] = best if best > b else b\n    return f[full]\n\n\ndef sstar(n, adj):\n    # closed neighbourhoods: N[A] = union of adj[v] | {v}\n    cl = [adj[v] | (1 << v) for v in range(n)]\n    NA = [0] * (1 << n); s1 = s2 = 0\n    for A in range(1, 1 << n):\n        low = A & -A; v = low.bit_length() - 1\n        NA[A] = NA[A ^ low] | cl[v]\n        a = bin(A).count(\"1\"); out = n - bin(NA[A]).count(\"1\")\n        t = min(a - 1, out); u = min(a, out)\n        if t > s1: s1 = t\n        if u > s2: s2 = u\n    return s1, s2\n\n\ndef one(line):\n    n, adj = parse_g6(line)\n    k = vs(n, adj); s1, s2 = sstar(n, adj)\n    return n, k, s1, s2\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(); ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=9); ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=16)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--selftest\", action=\"store_true\"); ap.add_argument(\"--min-n\", type=int, default=1); a = ap.parse_args()\n    if a.selftest:\n        import networkx as nx\n        from fixed_parameter_algorithm.pathwidth import compute_pathwidth\n        bad = 0; tot = 0\n        for n in range(2, 8):\n            for line in subprocess.run([\"nauty-geng\", \"-q\", str(n)], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.splitlines():\n                nn, adj = parse_g6(line); G = nx.from_graph6_bytes(line.encode())\n                tot += 1\n                if vs(nn, adj) != compute_pathwidth(G)[0]: bad += 1\n        print(f\"selftest: {tot} graphs to 7 vertices, {bad} pathwidth disagreements\"); return\n115:class Cell:\n123:    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n128:    def id(self) -> str:\n133:    def parse(text: str) -> \"Cell\":\n140:def cell_seed(cell: Cell, index: int) -> int:\n149:def instance_name(cell: Cell, index: int) -> str:\n153:def generate(cell: Cell, index: int) -> MOSPInstance:\n162:def pilot_cells(sizes=PILOT_N, ds=PILOT_D, ps=PILOT_P, m_ratio: int = 1) -> list[Cell]:\n171:def extension_cells(sizes=PILOT_N) -> list[Cell]:\n186:def analyse(instance: MOSPInstance, cell: Cell, index: int, solutions_dir: Path,\n243:def _job(args) -> dict:\n261:def write_manifest(frame: pd.DataFrame, path: Path = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"manifest.csv\") -> Path:\n270:def verify_manifest(path: Path = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"manifest.csv\",\n287:def load_results(csv: Path = RESULTS_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n293:def run(cells: list[Cell], per_cell: int, workers: int = 16,\n325:    def _flush(rows: list[dict]) -> None:\n366:def dedupe(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n372:def _cell_order(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n376:def cost_table(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n404:def cost_by_size(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n421:def config_ratio(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n437:def audit(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> dict[str, int]:\n458:def affordable(frame: pd.DataFrame, cells: list[Cell], hours: float = 2.5,\n501:def item02_cells(sizes=ITEM02_N, ratios=ITEM02_M_RATIOS, ds=ITEM02_D, ps=ITEM02_P) -> list[Cell]:\n532:def upward_cells(sizes=UPWARD_N, ratios=UPWARD_M_RATIOS, ds=UPWARD_D, ps=UPWARD_P) -> list[Cell]:\n545:def ridge100_cells(n: int = RIDGE100_N, ds=RIDGE100_D) -> list[Cell]:\n549:def price_ridge100(campaign_csv: Path = RESULTS_CSV, per_cell: int = RIDGE100_PER_CELL,\n589:def campaign_summary(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n610:def density_matrix(frame: pd.DataFrame, generator: str, ratio: int,\n640:def campaign_tables(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> str:\n657:def _md(frame: pd.DataFrame, floatfmt: str = \".3g\") -> str:\n661:def tables(frame: pd.DataFrame, hours: float = 2.5, workers: int = 16) -> str:\n687:def main() -> None:\n21:def build_customer_graph(instance: MOSPInstance) -> nx.Graph:\n22-    \"\"\"Build the customer intersection graph from a MOSP instance.\n23-\n24-    Args:\n25-        instance: A MOSPInstance with binary matrix M[customers x patterns].\n26-\n27-    Returns:\n28-        A NetworkX Graph where nodes are customer indices and edges connect\n29-        customers that share at least one pattern.\n30-    \"\"\"\n31-    G = nx.Graph()\n32-    n = instance.n_customers\n33-    G.add