ion 3.2: delete vertices of","+degree ≤ 1, suppress vertices of degree 2, until every degree is ≥ 3 or the","+graph is empty), and `τ(n) = o(n)` is the error term of Fomin & Høie's cubic","+bound, for which the paper gives no constant.","+","+Everything here is exact: `g` in `fractions.Fraction`, graphs as adjacency bit","+masks (`adj[v]` has bit `u` iff `u ~ v`), the reduction with a bucket of","+low-degree vertices so that it is linear in the number of steps (the dataset","+has graphs to 2,916 vertices). Removed vertices are *isolated*, as in the Lean","+design (plan §0.5): `reduce` returns the reduced adjacency on the same vertex","+set and the mask of removed vertices, and `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0` makes them","+weightless.","+","+Nothing here solves a pathwidth; the pathwidths come from the record.","+\"\"\"","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+import math","+from fractions import Fraction","+from functools import lru_cache","+from typing import Iterable","+","+__all__ = [","+    \"g\", \"g_float\", \"g_real\", \"g_prime\", \"alternating_factorial\", \"g_closed_form\",","+    \"popcount\", \"bits\", \"from_edges\", \"from_networkx\", \"degrees\", \"edge_count\",","+    \"components\", \"min_degree\", \"reduce\", \"main_term\", \"histogram_term\",","+    \"average_degree\", \"average_degree_term\", \"fminus\", \"f_potential\",","+    \"is_reduced\", \"is_cubic\", \"poisson_value\", \"fomin_hoie_n_eps\", \"fomin_hoie_budget\",","+]","+","+ALPHA = Fraction(1, 6)","+","+","+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------","+# the weights","+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------","+","+","+@lru_cache(maxsize=None)","+def g(n: int) -> Fraction:","+    \"\"\"`g_{1/6}(n)` in exact rationals; `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0`, `g(3) = 1/6`,","+    and `n g(n) = (n − 2) g(n − 1) + g(n − 2) + 1` for `n ≥ 4` (paper p. 6).\"\"\"","+    if n < 0:","+        raise ValueError(\"g is defined on the naturals\")","+    if n <= 2:","+        return Fraction(0)","+    if n == 3:","+        return ALPHA","+    return ((n - 2) * g(n - 1) + g(n - 2) + 1) / n","+","+","+def g_float(n: int) -> float:","+    return float(g(n))","+","+","+def g_real(x: float | Fraction) -> Fraction:","+    \"\"\"The paper's linear interpolation between integers (p. 6), exact when `x`","+    is a `Fraction`; below 2 it is 0, since `g(0) = g(1) = g(2) = 0`.\"\"\"","+    x = Fraction(x)","+    if x < 0:","+        raise ValueError(\"g_real is defined on x ≥ 0\")","+    n = math.floor(x)","+    t = x - n","+    return (1 - t) * g(n) + t * g(n + 1)","+","+","+def g_prime(n: int) -> Fraction:","+    \"\"\"`g'(n) = g(n) − g(n − 1)`; zero for `n ≤ 2` (and at 0).\"\"\"","+    if n <= 0:","+        return Fraction(0)","+    return g(n) - g(n - 1)","+","+","+def alternating_factorial(n: int) -> int:","+    \"\"\"`A(n) = n! − (n − 1)! + … ± 1!` (so `A(1) = 1`, `A(2) = 1`, `A(3) = 5`).\"\"\"","+    total = 0","+    sign = 1","+    for k in range(n, 0, -1):","+        total += sign * math.factorial(k)","+        sign = -sign","+    return total","+","+","+def g_closed_form(n: int, alpha: Fraction = ALPHA) -> Fraction:","+    \"\"\"Lemma 8.1: `g_α(n) = (4 − 3α) A(n)/n! + (2 − 3α)(−1)^n/n! − (3 − 3α)`, `n ≥ 2`.\"\"\"","+    if n < 2:","+        raise ValueError(\"the closed form is stated for n ≥ 2\")","+    fact = math.factorial(n)","+    return ((4 - 3 * alpha) * Fraction(alternating_factorial(n), fact)","+            + (2 - 3 * alpha) * Fraction((-1) ** n, fact) - (3 - 3 * alpha))","+","+","+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------","+# graphs as bit masks","+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------","+","+","+def popcount(x: int) -> int:","+    return x.bit_count()","+","+","+def bits(mask: int) -> Iterable[int]:","+    \"\"\"The set bits of `mask`, ascending.\"\"\"","+    while mask:","+        low = mask & -mask","+        yield low