{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgdBLiE9x32yqGQ6SoX5s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 01 is done and marked `- [x]`; the gate passed; `Current: 1/11 SOLVED`. The `main.pdf` change is the gate's own `make check` rebuild, as in earlier loops.\n\n**What was done**\n\n- **The manuscript** is at `reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/em2015.pdf` with text and SHA-256 (fetched 2026-11-02 00:26 UTC). Sections 1, 3, 5 and the Appendix agree word for word with the plan's quotations. Corollary 5.2 and Theorem 5.3 are on page 20, not 19. No discrepancy of substance.\n- **Code**: `learning/edwards_mcdermid.py` (exact `g`, `g'`, the bit-mask reduction, the three terms, `fminus`, the Poisson value, the Fomin–Høie budget) with 21 tests.\n- **The evaluation** covered every graph with a proved pathwidth, 63,330 in all, plus 4,681 cubic graphs to 16 vertices by the subset DP. Runtime 75 s. Report at `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §1.\n\n**Findings**\n\n- **No kill fired.** Zero graphs with `pw > main term + τ_FH(n)`, zero with `main term > histogram term`, no degree raised by the reduction.\n- **The main term alone bounds the pathwidth on 61.8% of the record.** The deficit never exceeds 5. The largest deficits are the 202-vertex VSPLIB trees at pathwidth 5, where the main term is zero: that is the paper's `O(log n)` term. Over graphs whose reduction is non-empty the maximum is 4.333, the Coxeter graph.\n- **The cubic base case needs a budget of 3.833 exhaustively to 16 vertices and 4.5 on the 42 certified cubic graphs to 120.** The record-holders are the small cages. Fomin–Høie's explicit budget is 2 to 100 times larger, so the corollary with that budget is vacuous at these sizes, as the plan predicted.\n- **The Poisson evaluation matches the pilot within 0.012 per vertex** at `n = 60–120`. The reduction's gain is 0.02 per vertex at `c = 3` and nothing from `c = 8`.\n- **Theorem 5.3's averaging lemma holds on all 52,747 graphs where it applies** and fails on 1,431 disconnected graphs below average degree 5, so its hypothesis is needed.\n- **A free audit passed**: the 13 dataset cubic graphs at 16 or fewer vertices match the exhaustive sweep by isomorphism, with agreeing pathwidths.\n\n**Next** is item 02, the exact statement with every intermediate lemma brute-forced on every graph to 9 vertices. The reduction and the per-component potential are ready for it in the module."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":790,"cache_read_input_tokens":227589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":790,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b959573-0e44-46cc-ba4e-13070f43883c","uuid":"9d5903e7-a893-4127-9afa-8cd0af9602f2","timestamp":"2026-11-02T00:47:04.974Z","request_id":"req_011CgdBLhqLQ1vzEgT5rbqW9"}
